{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## THE FIX WORKED, AND THE CREATE NOW FAILS ONE LAYER DEEPER — run 30870845838\n\nThe three field names Data Center originally rejected are **GONE from the run entirely**: `Field 'ticket_type'/'title'/'status' cannot be set` does not appear anywhere in run 30870845838. The bridge-schema leak is fixed and live-confirmed.\n\nThe create still 400s, but on a **different and more specific error**:\n\n    \"errors\":{\"priority\":\"Could not find valid 'id' or 'name' in priority object.\",\n               \"assignee\":\"data was not an object\"}\n\nThat is genuine progress rather than a wash: the payload now gets past field-name validation and fails on field SHAPE. Two of three original errors are eliminated and the survivors are a different class.\n\n### Root cause of the second layer\n\nBoth arrive as bare strings, and both for a reason:\n * the SHARED outbound mapper has already resolved rebar's integer priority to a Jira NAME (`LOCAL_PRIORITY_TO_JIRA` -> `\"Medium\"`), so a string reaches the transport;\n * Data Center identifies users by `name` rather than Cloud's accountId — which is why `validate_assignee_exists` returns the username on this transport.\n\nJira's REST API wants OBJECTS for both. ACLI accepts the bare forms, so the Cloud path never needed it. **That is the same per-transport seam a third time in one ticket** — the pass-through decision I approved for 'genuinely Jira-valid fields' was right about the NAMES and wrong about the SHAPES.\n\nFixed in Gerrit 1345: wrap only a non-empty **string**, so an already-object form is not nested a second time (a third distinct 400), and an absent field is never invented — injecting a default would assign the issue to nobody in particular, the create analogue of the mis-assignment bug 544e records on Cloud.\n\nGates: 2174 reconciler tests pass, ruff/mypy/hygiene clean.\n\n- [x] the failing STAGE is identified — dispatch, not bind\n- [x] the root cause is proven, not inferred — both layers, each named verbatim by Jira\n- [ ] the cell is GREEN on a live harness — needs the next run, with 1345 in it\n- [ ] an outbound create that fails to bind surfaces an operator-visible signal"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785812770389470001,"uuid":"168340a6-2b75-4f8d-821d-4d77a4bcac2a"}